<title>USA: Knoxville, Tenn., okays $12 million utility bonds.</title>
<headline>Knoxville, Tenn., okays $12 million utility bonds.</headline>
<dateline>KNOXVILLE, Tenn. 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Knoxville City Council approved the issuance of $12 million of revenue bonds for Knoxville Utility Board, Knoxville News-Sentinel reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>Bond proceeds will be used to expand natural gas service in the utility's service area.</p>
<p>Jim Carmon, head of the utlity's gas division, said increased demand was evenly distributed through the service area.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
